  "details": "Basically this should be a process that would allow for the avatar to be updated in the background. it should skip the entire description, image, and title process for updating an existing avatar and upload the assets in the background. This will also allow for the creator to make changes on others simultaneously and spend much less time waiting on an upload and more time making and fixing things. These updates should also be queueable. This means that, for example, say a user had a lot of avatars with a common problem and they fixed it for each of them (such as shader problems or old unity version). The user could then queue the updates to occur in order and also be able to cancel them individually or alltogether.",
